 "5204149623f2": {
  "gloss": "hateth",
  "tier": "B",
  "n": 4,
  "evidence": "1 John 4:20, named in the translation of 099r-099v: 'he that loveth not his brother whom he hath seen, how can he love God whom he hath not seen'. All four occurrences stand in that passage: 099v:4 reads 'brother [hateth], loves somebody how? this somebody God loves' almost word for word, 099r:10 and 099v:2 'brother [hateth] ... love'. hate is a word no sign carried (ktcross) and it is the one content word of the passage the pool tool (ktleft.py) left free that fits every line. One passage, so not A."
 },
 "5202b7": {
  "gloss": "became",
  "tier": "D",
  "n": 2,
  "evidence": "Genesis 2:7, 'and man became a living soul'. Both occurrences stand immediately before the codex's 'to-soul-one': 002v:10 'and [became] a living soul', 122r:3 '[became] a living soul, breathed on Adam'. become is carried by K&T's b30, but the passage pool (ktleft.py, Genesis 2:7 widened one verse) offered became as free and it is the only word of the verse that fits the slot both times. DOWNGRADED FROM C TO D on 2026-09-21 by the declared consequence of gate 4b in ktrederive.py. That gate masked 10% of K&T's dictionary and had a reading committed for 25 masked signs before anything was revealed. The declared bands said that a recovery rate of 15-30% means the judgment step adds little and that passage-read tier C entries should become D. The full sample scored 48%, but the test was INVALID: twelve of the 25 signs were ones whose K&T entry had already been seen in the same working session, and those scored 75% against 23% for the thirteen that had not. A blind test that is not blind measures nothing, so the 48% is discarded and the 23% on the clean subset is the estimate the consequence is applied to. This reading is NOT withdrawn and its evidence is unchanged; what has changed is the confidence label, which now says what it should have said: one line, one passage, no second occurrence to refuse it."
 },
